.TH "KC" "1" "Jan 0001" "kc dev" "kc Manual"

.SH NAME
kc-resolve - Resolve multiple secret IDs from stdin JSON and print values to stdout


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkc resolve [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Implements the Consi/OpenClaw exec provider protocol.

.PP
Reads a JSON request from stdin:
  {"protocolVersion":1,"provider":"kc","ids":["KEY1","KEY2"]}

.PP
Writes a JSON response to stdout:
  {"protocolVersion":1,"values":{"KEY1":"val1","KEY2":null}}

.PP
Unknown keys are returned as null. Protected keys trigger a single Touch ID
prompt before resolution. Use --no-touch-id to skip Touch ID for non-interactive
callers (e.g. Consi gateway startup).

.PP
Examples:
  echo '{"protocolVersion":1,"provider":"kc","ids":["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}' | kc resolve
  kc resolve --vault prod < request.json
  kc resolve --no-touch-id < request.json


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for resolve

.PP
\fB--no-touch-id\fP[=false]
	skip Touch ID authentication for protected keys


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--vault\fP=""
	target vault (overrides active vault)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkc(1)\fP
